   173	## 6. Final buttons and HA `[LOCKED]` (project_truth §4, D-50, D-54, D-57)
   174	- **Confirming… / Transferring… (D-81 F24–F25):** medicine rows and notes are read-only and muted, with no arrows. View Rx stays the outlined button (D-76).
   175	
   176	
   177	**Launch = Fallback B (D-83 CW-F1, D-85; Apurva 2026-11-03: the one Pilot flow).** Pilot live call → **Confirm prescription** (B1) → B2 checks for an HA → free: Transferring → **Transferred** (14) · none: **Forwarded** (B3). Pilot call ended before Confirm (16) or 7d → **Confirm & forward**. Skip HA → 17 → result path → Confirm prescription. Non-Value Meds go through the same HA check. The table below is **version A (later)**, where the route is known at call start.
   178	
   179	| Case type | HA status | Final button | Ending card |
   180	|---|---|---|---|
   181	| Cat4 | — | Confirm prescription | Prescription confirmed |
   182	| Pilot | HA skipped (by customer, system, or the doctor's Skip HA) | Confirm prescription | Prescription confirmed |
   183	| Pilot | Value meds, HA required | Confirm & transfer | Transferred to Health Advisor |
   184	| Pilot | Non-value meds, HA required | Confirm & forward | Forwarded to Health Advisor |
   185	
   186	**7d follows the route (CW-D2, D-83):** Cat4 / HA skipped → **Confirm prescription**; Pilot with an HA call → **Confirm & forward** (the transfer is no longer possible once the call has ended). Secondaries: **Callback + Unavailable**; no Skip HA on 7d. **Skip HA** on 8b, 12 and 16 sits full width under the main button (D-83, K1).
   187	
   188	- **Skip HA** only after the gate, for **both Pilot types** (Value and Non-Value Meds) whenever an HA call follows the doctor call and it isn't already skipped — no other conditions (D-59). Opens the reason sheet: Patient declined HA call · Clinically not required · Repeat patient, familiar with the medicines — Counselled in an earlier order (D-70 item 3; title and sub-line). Choosing a reason applies it at once. On a call with a result the final button becomes **Confirm prescription**; during a live transfer call the case then waits for the call result (state 17, D-58 point 14). Skip HA is also offered after a missed transfer (state 16, D-58 point 24).
   189	- Cat4 never shows anything about HA. HA-skipped Pilot never shows Transfer or Forward.
   190	- **Transfer vs forward** (D-57): transfer = the patient is handed to an HA on the same call; forward = an HA calls the patient back separately. A failed transfer goes as a forward; after Transferring (13) the doctor sees state 15 `call.transfer-failed` (CW-E1: the transfer couldn't start) — amber card "Forwarded to Health Advisor" with "Read the script, then end the call." (`call.transferFailed`) + script `call.forwardedTell` (§5, D-58 pts 17, 21, 23; MAIN-CHECK 2, D-85). No separate "HA didn't join" notice (D-58 pt 8 replaced by pts 15–17); the render id `t15-ha-no-join` is only a file name. A forward (15, B3) is confirmed only on the partner's result (CW-F2).
   191	- Confirm: button shows "Confirming…", everything else disabled, no second submit. Failure: notice in the bar "Couldn't confirm. Nothing was lost." (D-65). **Unclear result** (no answer from the server): the button stays on "Confirming…" — the same screen as `a-confirm-busy` — while the app checks; then it shows the confirmed card or the failure notice, never a second submit (D-69). An unclear result is checked before retrying (no double confirm).
   192	- **Analytics:** the four rows are four different outcomes and must stay separate events — never worked out from the button text (Cat4 and HA-skipped share a label). Event names are Engineering's choice `[LOCKED D-50]`.
   193	- What decides case type, value vs non-value, HA required and HA-skip eligibility comes from the backend `[OPEN — see CLAUDE.md "Never silently invent"]`.
   194	
   195	✅ **Flag 5 — answered (Apurva, 2026-10-16):** Confirm is blocked while any medicine is Pending. The button stays tappable; on tap a notice in the bar says "Prescribe or disable {n} medicines first." and the page scrolls to the first Pending medicine. Applies to all three confirm buttons; Callback, Skip HA and Unavailable stay allowed. *Original flag:* The old code lets the doctor confirm while some medicines are still Pending (not prescribed, not disabled). No decision covers this. Options: (a) block Confirm until every medicine is Prescribed or Disabled, with a note saying how many are left; (b) allow it, and Pending medicines are dropped from the prescription; (c) allow it with a confirmation sheet. Recommendation: (a) — a prescription with unreviewed medicines is a clinical risk.
