// Offline and phone Back on the Pilot stages
    96	
    97	**Empty case (D-80 pt 4, D-81 F23; D-83 CW-A6, K4):** no **Call patient**. An amber notice at the top of the panel says "No medicines on this order. Our Ops team will check it." (D-84; was "This order has no medicines. Release it — our Ops team will check it.") (where the released case goes is open, OQ-035). The main button is **Release case**, which releases directly (Releasing…, no sheet) and returns the doctor to Home (CW-A5). Header Back does the same. When Order details is hidden, View Rx is left-aligned (B-16).
    98	**Call ended, outcome card (D-81 F26, retired D-83):** the "End the call to get your next case." warning is retired with state 15b; after the hang-up the card is title only, neutral (MAIN-CHECK 2, D-85; `call.forwardedAfterHangup` retired, §14).
    99	**Bar and card rules (Round 4, 2026-11-02):** a bar notice that is the result of an action ("Couldn't confirm…", "Prescribe or disable…") sits inside the action bar above its button (RULES §9.5, A-19). Cards on the case page and Prescribe are 16 apart; the end-of-call script card has 16 padding below in every state (B-03, B-04, B-05). The callback-scheduled card uses the calendar icon and the patient-unavailable card the phone-off icon, the same icons as their buttons (B-22). A two-line patient name makes the header taller, not tighter (B-06). Long medicine titles wrap balanced (B-13).
   100	
   101	**Leaving a case:** the back-blocked toast breaks between its two sentences (B-21). An **attempted call** = leg 2 answered (the patient picked up) (D-58). Once a call is attempted, leaving is blocked until the case is closed (callback, unavailable, confirm). Before that, header **Back** opens the "Leave this case?" sheet — **Release case** (the case returns to the queue) or **Stay** (D-58 point 20, OQ-024; label D-84 CA-22; on Ready and states 3 and 4 only). Header Back is on 1, 3 and 4 only, while the patient has never been reached. It is hidden from the **Call patient** / **Call again** tap, incl. Calling 7a, the 7b question, Transfer, and the callback sheets, and never returns once the patient answered, also on a later 3 / 4 (D-80 pt 1, D-81 F21). Behind the leave sheet, Releasing… and Release failed the screen is **Ready** (D-81 F22). The backend refuses Release once our call request is accepted, unless the result is 3 or 4 (D-80). Release returns the doctor to Home (CW-A5). If the patient answered just before the tap, the backend refuses the release and the doctor stays on the case (`a-release-failed`, "Couldn't release this case. You're still on it."). The unassign action itself is a backend dependency (OQ-024). Help stays available at every stage and is the way to reach Doctor Ops when something keeps failing. App closed or phone off mid-case → reopening goes straight back into the case `[OPEN OQ-025, backend]`.
   102	
   103	**End-of-call script** (D-58 points 18, 21, 24 — copy keys in `messages.json`). Shown from the tap on Call while a call may be live; **hidden once the call has ended** (no one to read it to), except after a failed transfer (15) and B3, where the doctor is still on the line:
   104	- Launch B, Pilot live call (B1, neutral): `call.scriptNeutral` — "I'm writing your prescription now. Our Health Advisor will help you with the next steps."
   105	- Transfer (Pilot, Value Meds, version A — later): `call.scriptTransfer` — "I'm writing your prescription now. Please stay on the line — I'll connect you to our Health Advisor."
   106	- Forward (Pilot, Non-Value Meds, version A — later): `call.scriptForward` — "I'm writing your prescription now. Our Health Advisor will call you to help with the next steps."
   107	- Everything else (Cat4, HA skipped): `call.scriptCat4` — "I'm writing your prescription now. You can track your order in the Truemeds app."
   108	- After a failed transfer / no Health Advisor free: `call.forwardedTell` — "I've written your prescription. Our Health Advisor will call you back to help with the next steps." (one patient script for 15 and B3; the patient is never told about Health Advisor capacity).
   109	
   110	---
   111	
   112	## 5. Calls and the 50-second gate (D-58)
   113	
   114	**How a call works (first release).** One telecom partner at a time (Ozonetel or Knowlarity), click-to-call. Doctor taps **Call patient** → the partner rings the **doctor's phone first** (leg 1) → then the **patient** (leg 2). The doctor talks and ends the call **on the phone**; there is **no End call in the app**. The partner reports leg 1 and leg 2 separately.
   115	
   116	**Rules**
   117	- **Gate time is a setting** (today 50 s). Every message reads it — no "50" hard-coded in copy.
   118	- **Talk time adds up** across connected calls on the same case (each at least ~10 s, within ~30 min) — D-58 point 22. The doctor is never shown the count.
   119	- **Attempted call** = leg 2 answered. A failed request, a doctor who didn't answer, or a patient who didn't answer is not an attempted call.
   120	- **Launch B, Pilot live call:** our app counts from the moment the patient answers, while the call is live; at the gate time **Confirm prescription** (B1) appears on the live call. Our count is the truth; the partner's duration is stored for reporting only. (**Transfer cases** — Confirm & transfer on the live call, Pilot Value Meds — are version A, later.)
   121	- **All other cases** (Cat4, HA skipped, and Pilot calls that end before the gate or have no result): the next actions unlock only when the partner's call result arrives after the call ends.
   122	- **Before the gate, never show:** Confirm prescription, Confirm & transfer, Confirm & forward, Skip HA.
   123	- **Patient-side failure** (leg 2: no answer, busy, rejected, switched off, unreachable, invalid number), whenever it is detected: the case closes as **Patient unavailable** (state 9) by itself and goes on **hold**; the system retries it by hangup cause (CW-B1, CW-B2). **Doctor-side failure** (the doctor's leg, or a request refused for a reason that isn't the patient's number) stays on 3 / 4 (CW-B1). The doctor gets **Request next case** on 9.
   124	- **Transfer** (15, B3): 15 = the transfer couldn't start (no HA free, or the request failed); the doctor is still on the line. An HA who doesn't pick up is 14 for the doctor (CW-E1). While the call is live, 15 and B3 show only "Waiting for the call to end…"; after the hang-up, **Request next case · Back to Home** (CW-E3). A forward (15, B3) is confirmed only on the partner's result (CW-F2). **Launch: Fallback B first** (CW-F1).
   125	- **A call that's too short** (state 6) offers **Call again · Callback** (D-58 point 23). No retry limit. **Callback is offered only after the call: on 6 and on 7d** (CW-A1, CW-C3). The backend refuses a callback unless the patient answered (leg 2) (CW-A1).
   126	- **No call result** (state 7, D-58 point 20): at 3 min the bar asks "Are you still on the call?" **only when the app can't know the call has ended** (CW-D1); when the partner has already reported the hang-up, the 3-min timeout goes straight to 7c. After "Call ended" and a backend check with nothing found: **Confirm prescription** (Cat4) or **Confirm & forward** (Pilot), with **Callback · Unavailable** (CW-D2). Confirm there shows "Waiting for the call record" until the record arrives (D-68); a record under the gate, or no record after a wait time, means the prescription is **not confirmed** → hold and retry (CW-D3, CW-D4). Nothing goes to Ops. A late result updates the screen by itself. Repeated problems → the doctor uses **Help** on the case.
   127	- **Callback on a live call is refused by the backend** unless the patient answered (leg 2); the sheet then shows "Couldn’t schedule a callback. The patient wasn’t reached." (CW-A1, K3).
   128	- **Vendor terms are mapped by Engineering** to the buckets in the table (Ozonetel `CustomerStatus`, Knowlarity hangup causes — `projects/ACOM/ring-ai/reference/knowlarity-hangup-causes.pdf`).
   129	
   130	**State table (final, 2026-10-24 — D-58 points 14–22; rows changed by the calling round are per D-83, see §14).** One row per state. Render id = recipe in `docs/renders/2026-10-22-calling/src/case.html`. Copy keys in `ui-screens/feedback/messages.json`. During every call the End-of-call script shows under Order details. Callback is offered only on 6 and 7d (D-83 CW-A1).
   131	
   132	| # | State ID | State | Trigger (from the backend, by polling) | Bar (top → bottom) | Render id |
   133	|---|---|---|---|---|---|
   134	| 1 | `call.ready` | Ready to call | Case opened | Call patient · header Back (leave sheet) | `t01-ready` |
   135	| 2 | `call.calling` | Calling (whole call) = 7a | Doctor taps Call; until a result | "Calling {name}…" status line only · no Callback (CW-A1) · no header Back (D-81 F21) | `t02-calling` / `s7a-calling` |
   136	| 3 | `call.not-through` | Didn't go through | Request refused, or leg-1 network/vendor error | Red notice · Call again · header Back | `t03-not-through` |
   137	| 4 | `call.doctor-missed` | You didn't answer | Leg 1 not answered / busy / rejected | Amber notice · Call again · header Back | `t04-doctor-missed` |
   138	| 5 | `call.result-wait` | Getting call result | Partner reported the hang-up (Pilot), result not in yet. Cat4 never reaches 5 (CW-C2) | "Getting call result…" status line only · no Callback (CW-C1) | `t05-result-wait` |
   139	| 6 | `call.ended-early` | Call too short | Result: total talk time on the case under the gate | Amber "Call too short…" · Call again · Callback (no Unavailable — D-58 point 23) | `t06-ended-early` |
